package practice

// BitManipulationDrills are the bit manipulation foundations, a ladder from
// representation to tricks: write a number in binary (n % 2 and n // 2), read a
// binary string (shift and add), get, set, clear and toggle one bit with a
// mask, Power of Two (n & (n - 1)), the positions of the set bits (n & -n
// isolates the lowest one), Hamming Distance (XOR, then count) and Single
// Number III (split on one bit where two numbers differ), and last subsets
// listed by bitmask in mask order. They build up to Number of 1 Bits, Counting
// Bits, Reverse Bits and Sum of Two Integers in the ladder without repeating
// them, and each explanation says why the identity holds. They follow
// docs/pedagogy.md like any problem.
